{"shortDescription":"Basis bids for hard red winter wheat were unchanged in the southern US Plains on Friday, spot checks showed, and cash markets were quiet as wheat futures dropped and farmers focused on planting the 2027 winter wheat crop, merchandisers said.Basis values are quoted against futures in cts/bu:NOTES: U…","astDescription":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"p","children":["Basis bids for hard red winter wheat were unchanged in the southern US Plains on Friday, spot checks showed, and cash markets were quiet as wheat futures dropped and farmers focused on planting the 2027 winter wheat crop, merchandisers said."]},{"type":"list","children":[{"type":"*","children":[{"type":"p","children":["Warm and dry weather this week has helped accelerate seeding following heavy rains at the start of the month. \"Guys are running hard, putting wheat in the ground,\" one Oklahoma merchandiser said."]}]},{"type":"*","children":[{"type":"p","children":["High temperatures neared 90 degrees Fahrenheit (32 degrees Celsius) on Friday as far north as South Dakota."]}]},{"type":"*","children":[{"type":"p","children":["\"Warmth is ideal for the germination and establishment of recently planted winter grains, especially in areas noting recent improvements in topsoil moisture,\" the US Department of Agriculture said in a daily weather note."]}]},{"type":"*","children":[{"type":"p","children":["K.C. December hard red winter wheat (KWZ26) futures settled down 17 cents on Friday, or 2.3%, at $7.19-1/4 per bushel after hitting $7.09, the contract's lowest since mid-July."]}]},{"type":"*","children":[{"type":"p","children":["Wheat fell in sympathy with corn and soybean futures after the USDA hiked its 2026 US harvest outlook."]}]},{"type":"*","children":[{"type":"p","children":["The USDA also raised its forecast of US 2026/27 wheat ending stocks to 740 million bushels, up from 717 million last month and above the average analyst estimate of 721 million."]}]},{"type":"*","children":[